    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="18e763bf-3e1c-5040-8e29-6b9140cf1d34" activityNameId="4b55ae9d-817c-5173-867b-b4ca98f49023" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Disposal, building, door, outer, wood-glass, to final disposal</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Disposal, building, door, outer, wood-glass, to final disposal
The dataset can be applied for a standard outer door (wood-glass) disposal process in Switzerland. Disposal of glazing linked to updated dataset from QualiBob project. Philippe Stolz, September 2016.\nGeography: Dataset represents standard in Europe and/or Switzerland.\nTechnology: The technology in this dataset represents standard incineration technology in Europe. \nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Entsorgungssysteme\nLocal subcategory: Gebäudeentsorgung\nUVEK 2022 source file:07156.XML\n\n
UUID: 3e9b02dc-bddd-4ac5-a384-53b5a3c112b9
The dataset describes the disposal of a wood-glass outer door in a municipal incineration. The door frame out of steel is recycled at 100%. The rest of the materials (rest of steel parts, aluminium, rubber, plastics, mortar, paints and wood) is disposed in a municipal solid waste incineration. 
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The technology in this dataset represents standard incineration technology in Europe. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Calculation from waste composition 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3e9b02dc-bddd-4ac5-a384-53b5a3c112b9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
